# Act 1, chapter 4 "The First Androids" (flags 320 opening seen, 321-323 relays, 324 power restored, 325 Android 16
# shelved, 326 Gero is Android 20, 327 Prototype 12 destroyed). Bunker rooms: 1:72 main lab, 1:74 tank room, 1:76 incubator, 1:78 split pod.
list ch4_start
set_flag 320
do call 183 516 1456 1457
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1; call 165 0 20
do call 120 1; call 119 1 72 1 112 200; call 121 60
narrate Years later. The bunker in the northern mountains.
say young_gero.0 Prototypes one through twelve. Failures, every one of them.
say young_gero.3 Sixteen will be different... if this bunker stays powered long enough to wake him. Three relays, dead again.
say young_gero.0 One relay is here. The other two are out in the old mine workings, and the mountain is full of my failures.
narrate Gero powers up the one drone he salvaged from headquarters. It still has the army's colours.
# the salvaged drone: Energy Blast and Energy Punch only (see act1_ch1.scene lab_terminal)
do call 151 2; call 149 2; call 152 0
do call 165 2 20; call 165 2 16
journal Restore power: three {c07}relays{c02}, one in the bunker and two outside
do call 47; call 51 0
list relay_1
unless_flag 320 relay_idle1
if_flag 321 relay_done1
set_flag 321
narrate The corroded relay snaps closed. Sparks, then a steady hum. One relay online.
run ch4_power
stop
label relay_idle1
narrate An old Red Ribbon terminal, thick with dust.
stop
label relay_done1
narrate The relay hums steadily.
list relay_2
unless_flag 320 relay_idle2
if_flag 322 relay_done2
set_flag 322
narrate A relay node is wired into the cave wall. Its breaker snaps back into place. One relay online.
run ch4_power
stop
label relay_idle2
narrate A Red Ribbon relay node, dark and silent. Gero hasn't asked for power yet.
stop
label relay_done2
narrate The relay hums steadily.
list relay_3
unless_flag 320 relay_idle3
if_flag 323 relay_done3
unless_flag 290 relay_guard3
set_flag 323
narrate The mine's relay node sparks back to life as the drone splices the frayed cables. One relay online.
run ch4_power
stop
label relay_idle3
narrate A Red Ribbon relay node, dark and silent. Gero hasn't asked for power yet.
stop
label relay_done3
narrate The relay hums steadily.
stop
label relay_guard3
narrate The relay node is wedged under Prototype 9's bulk. The drone can't reach the cables while that thing is still moving.
# all three relays (and not announced before) -> power restored
list ch4_power
unless_flag 321 power_no
unless_flag 322 power_no
unless_flag 323 power_no
if_flag 324 power_no
set_flag 324
narrate Deep below, the generators roar back to life. Every light in the bunker comes on at once.
narrate Then, from the incubator: the shriek of tearing metal.
# Prototype 12 (enemy row 34, spawns in the incubator 1:76 while 324 is set and 327 clear): Gero sends the drone in. Its death script
# sets 327.
do call 151 2; call 149 2
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 76 1 120 264; call 121 40
narrate Prototype 12 has torn itself out of the conversion pod!
say young_gero.1 Twelve?! I scrapped you years ago... Drone! Destroy it before it wrecks everything!
journal Destroy {c07}Prototype 12{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
label power_no
list a16_talk
if_flag 325 a16_shelved
unless_flag 324 a16_dark
unless_flag 327 a16_wait
do call 149 0
set_flag 325
narrate Prototype 12 is scrap metal on the incubator floor. Gero turns to the last pod.
say young_gero.3 Now. Let us wake him.
narrate Android 16's eyes flicker open.
say android16 ...Where am I?
say young_gero.0 In my laboratory. You are Android 16. Run your combat routine. Destroy the drone.
say android16 I do not want to destroy it. It has done nothing wrong.
say young_gero.1 It is a machine! You are a machine! Obey me!
say android16 I would rather watch the birds outside. Are there birds here?
say young_gero.2 That face. That voice. I gave you my son's face... and you took his heart as well.
say young_gero.0 Too gentle. Like him. You will never kill Goku.
narrate Gero powered Android 16 down and sealed him away. He would not wake again for many years.
say young_gero.1 If no machine can carry my hatred, then I will carry it myself.
journal Enter the conversion pod in the {c07}incubator{c02}
stop
label a16_wait
narrate Android 16 stands motionless. Prototype 12 first!
stop
label a16_dark
narrate Android 16 stands motionless. Without power, its eyes are dark.
stop
label a16_shelved
narrate Android 16, powered down. Gevo's face, sleeping.
list ch4_pod
unless_flag 325 pod_wait
set_flag 326
narrate Gero lies down in the conversion pod and starts the procedure on himself.
say young_gero.0 Flesh fails. Flesh grows old. Flesh mourns.
do call 120 60
do call 120 1; call 119 1 78 1 184 260; call 121 60
narrate Nine hours later, the pod split open.
say gero Android 20. I feel nothing at all. Good.
say gero Now I have all the time in the world. Goku... I will build the soldiers that finish you.
# Androids 13-15 (BF's leftover scouter text: "An evil Android created by Dr. Gero's computer."): Gero hands the designs
# to the lab's supercomputer, as in the film. They return in Act 3.
say gero Computer. Begin construction on designs thirteen, fourteen and fifteen.
narrate The bunker's great computer wakes. On its screens, three new androids begin to take shape.
say gero Whatever becomes of me, finish them. Their only purpose: Goku's death.
# the army files stay with Gero (native 130 = take one item; only as many as were read)
unless_flag 510 fc0
do call 130 29
label fc0
unless_flag 511 fc1
do call 130 29
label fc1
unless_flag 512 fc2
do call 130 29
label fc2
unless_flag 513 fc3
do call 130 29
label fc3
unless_flag 514 fc4
do call 130 29
label fc4
unless_flag 515 fc5
do call 130 29
label fc5
narrate End of Act One.
do call 120 60
# Act 2: West City; chapter 5's opening fires on arrival (flag 300 clear) and plays its own card and fade-in
do call 120 1; call 119 4 1 1 268 296
stop
label pod_wait
narrate The conversion pod. Gero has not dared to use it yet.
# ---------- outside the bunker (areas from log4/gen_ch4.py; flags 289-292)
list ch4_pass
set_flag 289
narrate The mountain pass. Somewhere in these hills, Gero dumped every prototype he couldn't fix.
say young_gero.1 Some of them still have power. I never did like waste... and they never did learn to obey.
do call 47; call 51 0
list cache_gen
if_flag 291 gen_empty
set_flag 291
narrate An old Red Ribbon locker, rusted shut. The drone pries it open: two sodas and a Senzu Bean.
do call 129 2 2; call 129 11 1
stop
label gen_empty
narrate The locker is empty.
list cache_mine
if_flag 292 mine_empty
set_flag 292
narrate A mining cart full of junk. Under it all: a bottle of tea and a carton of milk.
do call 129 1 1; call 129 0 1
stop
label mine_empty
narrate Nothing but rocks.
# ---------- the Old Mine's barred gate (1:110 and 17:39, examine facing up): tells the player the shaft is no exit
list mine_gate
narrate An iron gate bars the old shaft. Beyond it the tunnel has fallen in: rock and rotten beams, all the way down.
stop
# ---------- the prototype graveyard (areas from log4/gen_more.py; flags 455 arrival, 456 Prototype 3 destroyed,
# 457 cache). Gero speaks over the drone's radio.
list ch4_graveyard
set_flag 455
narrate A canyon below the pass. Rusted shapes lie everywhere: torsos, arms, heads half buried in the scree.
narrate Gero's failures. Twelve years of them, dumped here one by one.
say young_gero.1 Don't waste time down there. They're scrap. Every one of them failed me.
narrate Something among the wrecks lifts its head. Its eye lights up red.
say young_gero.2 ...Prototype 3. It shouldn't have any power left. Put it down.
journal Destroy {c07}Prototype 3{c02} in the graveyard
do call 47; call 51 0
list wreck_1
narrate Prototype 1. The plate on its chest reads FIRST MODEL. COULD NOT STAND.
narrate Next to the words, in grease pencil, someone has drawn a smiling face. A child's drawing.
say young_gero.0 Gevo drew that. He was six. He said it looked lonely.
list wreck_5
narrate Prototype 5. The file said it obeyed every order perfectly.
narrate It was ordered to guard the lab. It found its own reflection in a window and fired at it for three days.
list wreck_8
narrate Prototype 8's voice box still holds a charge. When the drone touches it, it plays a recording.
narrate A young man, laughing: "Dad! It's working! It said my name!" Then static.
say young_gero.3 ...Leave that one alone.
list cache_grave
if_flag 457 cgrave_empty
set_flag 457
narrate A Red Ribbon crate, stove in. Inside, packed in straw: an Elixir and two root beers.
do call 129 7 1; call 129 5 2
stop
label cgrave_empty
narrate An empty crate.
# ---------- army files 5 and 6 (flags 514 / 515)
list file_grave
if_flag 514 fgrave_read
set_flag 514
narrate Under this wreck: a soldier's field pack, and a diary.
narrate "Drew guard duty at the old scientist's bunker. He talks to the robots at night. Like they're his sons."
narrate The last entry: "Transferred out tomorrow. Good. I don't think he'd notice if I died up here."
do call 129 29 1
run files_check
stop
label fgrave_read
narrate A rusted wreck. The soldier's pack is gone.
list file_cave
if_flag 515 fcave_read
set_flag 515
narrate Army file: a radio log, still on the relay desk. The last entry:
narrate "To all units. Headquarters destroyed. Commander Red is dead. The Red Ribbon Army is dissolved. Go home."
say young_gero.1 Home.
do call 129 29 1
run files_check
stop
label fcave_read
narrate The radio log. The army's last order.
# all six army files read -> files_done (once, flag 516)
list files_check
unless_flag 510 files_not_yet
unless_flag 511 files_not_yet
unless_flag 512 files_not_yet
unless_flag 513 files_not_yet
unless_flag 514 files_not_yet
unless_flag 515 files_not_yet
if_flag 516 files_not_yet
run files_done
label files_not_yet
list files_done
set_flag 516
narrate Six army files. The whole Red Ribbon Army in one thin folder.
narrate A commander who wanted to be taller. An officer who shot him for it. A son who asked them not to tell his father.
say young_gero.2 Fools. Every one of them. Only the machines ever did as they were told.
narrate Clipped inside the last file: two vials from the army's medical stores. Experimental. Never approved.
do call 129 10 2
narrate Got two Holy Waters.
# ---------- exit audit 2026-11-03
list grave_drop
set_flag 447
narrate The trail ends at a sheer drop into the canyon. Down there: more scrap, and no way back up.
